    <section id="warnings" class="card p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24 border-l-8 border-l-caci-purple">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-4 mb-6">
            <span class="badge mb-1">Daniel &amp; Revelation</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold">14. Prophetic Warnings: Changing Times and Laws</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-4 mb-6">
            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister text-sm block mb-1">
                    <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/dan/7/25" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Daniel 7:25 (KJV) &nearr;</a>
                </span>
                <blockquote class="scripture-quote text-slate-700 text-xs leading-relaxed">
                    &ldquo;And he shall speak great words against the most High, and shall wear out the saints of the most High, <strong class="text-caci-red font-bold">and think to change times and laws:</strong> and they shall be given into his hand until a time and times and the dividing of time.&rdquo;
                </blockquote>
                <div class="mt-2 text-xs text-slate-600">
                    Aramaic: <em>Zman</em> (appointed seasons/feasts) and <em>Dath</em> (divine laws/commandments). Daniel foresaw an earthly power attempting to alter God's calendar and commandments!
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister text-sm block mb-1">
                    <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/rev/18/4" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Revelation 18:4 (KJV) &nearr;</a>
                </span>
                <blockquote class="scripture-quote text-slate-700 text-xs leading-relaxed">
                    &ldquo;And I heard another voice from heaven, saying, <strong class="text-caci-minister font-bold">Come out of her, my people, that ye be not partakers of her sins, and that ye receive not of her plagues.</strong>&rdquo;
                </blockquote>
            </div>

            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister text-sm block mb-1">
                    <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/2th/2/3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">2 Thessalonians 2:3&ndash;12 (The Falling Away &amp; Strong Delusion) &nearr;</a>
                </span>
                <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 italic">
                    Paul warned that before Yeshua returns there would be a falling away (apostasy) and the revelation of the lawless one. Those who do not receive the love of the truth fall victim to strong delusion.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 border-t-2 border-caci-purple p-4 rounded-b-lg text-sm text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-caci-minister">Key Understanding:</strong>
            Scripture warned us that an earthly system would seek to change God's appointed times and laws. In these last days, God calls His people out of religious Babylon back to His pure, unadulterated covenant.
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PRACTICAL GUIDE: HOW DO WE KEEP THE SABBATH TODAY? -->
    <section id="practical-guide" class="card p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24 border-l-8 border-l-amber-500 bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-50/40 via-white to-slate-50">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-4 mb-6">
            <span class="badge uppercase tracking-wider bg-amber-100 text-amber-900 border border-amber-200 mb-1">Living the Commandment</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-caci-blue">How Do We Keep the Sabbath Today? A Practical Walkout Guide</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-2">
                The Sabbath was given as a weekly sanctuary in time—a day of physical rest, spiritual renewal, family fellowship, and holy assembly. Here is how believers walk it out according to Scripture:
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-5 mb-6">
            <!-- 1. Sunset to Sunset -->
            <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between border-t-4 border-t-caci-blue">
                <div>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-blue-100 text-caci-blue flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs">1</span>
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-caci-blue">Sunset to Sunset</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
                        In biblical timekeeping, the biblical day begins at evening. The Sabbath begins Friday at sundown and concludes Saturday at sundown.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-semibold text-caci-minister">
                    <span>Genesis 1:5 &middot; Leviticus 23:32</span>
                    <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/lev/23/32" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-caci-tone2 hover:underline">KJV &nearr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 2. Cease From Work & Commerce -->
            <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between border-t-4 border-t-caci-purple">
                <div>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-purple-100 text-caci-purple flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs">2</span>
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-caci-blue">Cease From Regular Work &amp; Commerce</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
                        Step away from weekday employment, worldly business, buying, and selling. It is a day to set down our labors and be physically refreshed in God's provision.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-semibold text-caci-minister">
                    <span>Exodus 20:10 &middot; Nehemiah 10:31</span>
                    <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/exo/20/10" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-caci-tone2 hover:underline">KJV &nearr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 3. Gather for Holy Convocation -->
            <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between border-t-4 border-t-amber-500">
                <div>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs">3</span>
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-caci-blue">Gather for Holy Convocation</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
                        The Sabbath is a commanded <em>Miqra Kodesh</em> (sacred assembly). Assemble with fellow believers in person or online to worship, pray, read Scripture, and sit under the Word.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-semibold text-caci-minister">
                    <span>Leviticus 23:3 &middot; Luke 4:16</span>
                    <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/lev/23/3" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-caci-tone2 hover:underline">KJV &nearr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- 4. Make It a Delight -->
            <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between border-t-4 border-t-[#C8102E]">
                <div>
                    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
                        <span class="w-7 h-7 rounded-full bg-red-100 text-[#C8102E] flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs">4</span>
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-base text-caci-blue">Make It a Delight</h3>
                    </div>
                    <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
                        Share a special Sabbath meal, extend mercy, visit the lonely or sick, and focus on family and the Lord rather than legalistic restrictions. The Sabbath was made for man!
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between text-xs font-semibold text-caci-minister">
                    <span>Isaiah 58:13&ndash;14 &middot; Mark 2:27</span>
                    <a href="https://www.blueletterbible.org/kjv/isa/58/13" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-caci-tone2 hover:underline">KJV &nearr;</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-amber-50/80 border-t-2 border-amber-500 p-4 rounded-b-lg text-sm text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-caci-minister">Pastoral Counsel:</strong>
            Transitioning to the biblical Sabbath is a joyful journey of walking in covenant obedience. Begin where you are: set aside Friday evening for family prayer and Scripture, step away from commercial transactions, and join with us on Saturday as we celebrate Messiah's day of rest.
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 15. WHAT IS TRUTH? -->
    <section id="what-is-truth" class="card p-6 md:p-8 scroll-mt-24 border-l-8 border-l-caci-blue">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200 pb-4 mb-6">
            <span class="badge mb-1">The Definition of Truth</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold">15. What Is Truth? Loving God by Keeping His Commandments</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200 text-xs">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister block mb-1">John 17:17</span>
                <p class="italic text-slate-700">&ldquo;Sanctify them through thy truth: thy word is truth.&rdquo;</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200 text-xs">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister block mb-1">Psalm 119:151&ndash;152</span>
                <p class="italic text-slate-700">&ldquo;Thou art near, O LORD; and all thy commandments are truth. Concerning thy testimonies, I have known of old that thou hast founded them for ever.&rdquo;</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200 text-xs">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister block mb-1">John 14:15 &amp; 1 John 5:3</span>
                <p class="italic text-slate-700">&ldquo;If ye love me, keep my commandments... For this is the love of God, that we keep his commandments: and his commandments are not grievous.&rdquo;</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200 text-xs">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister block mb-1">1 John 2:3&ndash;4</span>
                <p class="italic text-slate-700">&ldquo;And hereby we do know that we know him, if we keep his commandments. He that saith, I know him, and keepeth not his commandments, is a liar, and the truth is not in him.&rdquo;</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200 text-xs">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister block mb-1">Revelation 14:12</span>
                <p class="italic text-slate-700">&ldquo;Here is the patience of the saints: here are they that keep the commandments of God, and the faith of Jesus.&rdquo;</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded border border-slate-200 text-xs">
                <span class="font-bold text-caci-minister block mb-1">Revelation 22:14</span>
                <p class="italic text-slate-700">&ldquo;Blessed are they that do his commandments, that they may have right to the tree of life, and may enter in through the gates into the city.&rdquo;</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 border-t-2 border-caci-blue p-5 rounded-b-lg text-sm text-slate-800 leading-relaxed space-y-3">
            <p>
                Jesus declared that the greatest commandment is to love God with all our heart, soul, mind, and strength, and the second is to love our neighbor as ourselves. The first four commandments (including the Sabbath) reveal <strong>how we love God</strong>, and the last six reveal <strong>how we love our neighbor</strong>.
            </p>
            <p>
                The Seventh Day Sabbath is the only day God set apart from the foundation of the world. It is the day He commanded us to cease from worldly labor and assemble in holy convocation. It is a sign between God and His people, and a weekly dress rehearsal for the seventh millennium—the Millennial Reign of Yeshua (2 Peter 3:8).
            </p>
            <p class="font-bold text-caci-minister">
                God never abolished nor changed the Sabbath. He told us: &ldquo;Remember the Sabbath day, to keep it holy.&rdquo; God does not change, and His commandments endure forever.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CALL TO OBSERVE WITH US -->
    <section class="scripture-card text-center p-8 md:p-12">
        <span class="label">WORSHIP WITH US ON THE SABBATH</span>
        <h3 class="text-2xl md:text-4xl font-bold font-head text-white mt-2 mb-4">Experience the Blessing of Sabbath Rest</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-200 max-w-2xl mx-auto text-sm md:text-base mb-3 leading-relaxed">
            Join @_profile.CongregationName every Sabbath as we enter into His rest, study the Whole Counsel of God, and fellowship together.
        </p>
        <p class="text-amber-300 font-semibold text-xs md:text-sm mb-6">
            Join us in person in Southwest Missouri or online every Saturday (Prayer 12:00 PM &middot; Service 12:30 PM Central)
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
            <a href="@($"/congregation/{_profile.UrlSlug}/what-we-believe")" class="btn-secondary">What We Believe</a>
            <a href="@($"/congregation/{_profile.UrlSlug}/feasts")" class="btn-secondary">Biblical Feasts Calendar</a>
            <a href="@($"/congregation/{_profile.UrlSlug}/connect?")from=Sabbath%20Teaching%20Page" class="btn-primary">Connect With Us</a>
        </div>
    </section>

</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string Slug { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    protected override async Task OnParametersSetAsync()
    {
        if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Slug))
        {
            TenantContext.SetSlug(Slug);
        }
        _profile = await CongregationService.GetCurrentAsync();
    }

    private CongregationProfile _profile = new();

    private static readonly IReadOnlyList<CongregationSeoHead.FaqItem> SabbathFaqs = new CongregationSeoHead.FaqItem[]
    {
        new(
            "Does Romans 14 abolish the Seventh-Day Sabbath?",
            "No. The Sabbath is never mentioned in Romans 14. The entire chapter deals with vegetarianism vs eating meat, wine, and voluntary days of fasting. Paul was instructing Jewish and Gentile believers not to judge one another over personal dietary customs or fast days, not repealing the Fourth Commandment."
        ),
        new(
            "Does Galatians 4:8-10 warn against observing the biblical Sabbath and God's feasts?",
            "No. In verse 8 Paul explicitly addresses Gentiles who previously 'did service unto them which by nature are no gods' and had never kept the biblical Sabbath. Paul was warning them against reverting to pagan Roman and Greek astrological calendars and lucky/unlucky days. Scripture never calls God's holy commandments 'weak and beggarly elements.'"
        ),
        new(
            "What was nailed to the cross in Colossians 2:14-17?",
            "The Greek term cheirographon refers to the handwritten certificate of debt—our record of sins, guilt, and transgressions. Messiah blotted out the penalty of our sin on the cross, not the moral Law that defines what sin is. Furthermore, verse 17 states these holy appointed days 'are a shadow of things to come' (present tense), foreshadowing Messiah's millennial reign."
        )
    };
}



